### PAR-028 | recovery: two independent syntax errors (one in decls, one in a graph body)
input good: Tensor[a=1]
weight bad
graph g {
  m = good
  n p
  return m
}

### PAR-029 | recovery: two independent malformed statements in the same graph body
graph g {
  a b
  ok1 = m
  ok2 = n
  c d
  return ok2
}

### PAR-030 | diagnostics: SourceSpan of a missing-token error points at the offending token
graph g {
b c
return b
}

### PAR-031 | regression: bare int literal as a binop operand reports a diagnostic, not a crash
graph g {
  a = x * 2
  return a
}

### PAR-032 | regression: an illegal axis dimSize token reports a diagnostic, not a crash
input x: Tensor[y=@]
graph g { return x }

### BND-PAR-001 | graph body that is only return (zero statements) vs a single statement
graph empty1 { return z }
graph one1 { w = z
 return w }

### BND-PAR-002 | minimal legal program: zero decls, exactly one graph, return-only body
graph onlyreturn { return z }

